WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.100
WHY HOLLYWOOD WON'T CAST BRENDAN FRASER ANYMORE

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:10.699
There was a time when actor Brendan Fraser
was starring in multiple movies regularly.

00:00:10.699 --> 00:00:15.150
Those days are long, long gone. Where did
it all go wrong for the Indianapolis-born

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.700
actor? Let's count the ways Dudley Do-Right
started doing so little.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.140
BOMBING AT THE BOX OFFICE

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:27.130
Fraser had a rough 2010, and that year may
be why he's become persona non grata in Hollywood.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.879
In the span of two months, Fraser starred
in two box office disasters. The medical drama

00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:37.469
Extraordinary Measures was universally panned
by critics, who said it belonged on television.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:42.220
Audiences stayed home, and it earned just
$12 million off a $31 million budget. Three

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.370
months later, Fraser starred in Furry Vengeance.
Compared to Extraordinary Measures, Furry

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:54.280
Vengeance performed about the same, grossing
$17.6 million off a $35 million budget. Unfortunately

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.579
for Fraser, the film was universally crushed
by critics.

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:00.950
KILLED HIS OWN COMEBACK

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.689
Fraser's kid-friendly action flick, Journey
to the Center of the Earth, was a surprise

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:09.820
hit. It become one of the highest-grossing
movies of 2008, earning an impressive $101.7

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:16.479
million. New Line Cinema wanted a sequel—fast.
But Fraser wanted to hold out for the original's

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:21.729
director, Eric Brevig, who was busy finishing
Yogi Bear 3-D. The studio decided to use a

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:26.020
new director and replaced Fraser with Dwayne
"The Rock" Johnson. On the one hand, Fraser's

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.960
loyalty was admirable; on the other, his timing
couldn't have been worse. Johnson replaced

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.710
Fraser only months after Furry Vengeance bombed
in theaters, a time when Fraser desperately

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.780
needed better work.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.010
THE MUMMY FRANCHISE LIMPED ON

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:45.290
The first Mummy movie from 1999, while not
a hit with critics, earned a massive $155

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.950
million in theaters. The sequel, The Mummy
Returns, was an even bigger hit, grossing

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:55.670
a staggering $202 million in 2001, and making
it one of the 10 highest-grossing movies that

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.970
year. One would think that Universal Pictures
would try to rush out a threequel. But because

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:04.700
of various delays, the third Mummy didn't
arrive until 2008, with a new director and

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.729
an almost entirely new cast on board. By then,
audiences had grown tired of the franchise,

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.989
especially after the Scorpion King spin-off.
That fatigue showed in the film's performance.

00:02:13.989 --> 00:02:18.890
It barely crossed $100 million in the U.S.,
signaling the beginning of the end. The Mummy

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.400
had decayed.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.520
LACKLUSTER PROJECTS

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:27.020
Some of Fraser's biggest flops included the
live-action adaptation of Dudley Do-Right,

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:33.060
which grossed a paltry $9.9 million off a
$70 million budget; the bizarre 2001 comedy

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:38.760
Monkeybone, which earned just $5.4 million
off a $75 million budget; and Looney Tunes:

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:44.500
Back in Action, which took in $20.9 million
off an $80 million budget. At the time, Fraser

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.099
was lucky with The Mummy franchise to counter
these flops.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:50.069
HIS WEIRD GOLDEN GLOBES CLAP

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:55.010
Fraser became the subject of humorous GIFs,
memes, and general Internet ridicule after

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:58.930
cameras caught him awkwardly laughing and
clapping while Robert De Niro was presenting

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:04.140
the Cecil B. DeMille Award at the 2010 Golden
Globes. The three-second-long moment had everyone

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.250
laughing the night of the ceremony; video
remixes, including one set to Gwen Stefani's

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:21.239
"Hollaback Girl," made it the stuff of Internet
legend. Once the affable star of innocuous

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:26.390
Hollywood movies, Fraser looked awkward and
somewhat out of place. It's okay Brendan,

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.750
we'll still give you an awkward ovation.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.420
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to see more videos like the one you

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:36.480
just saw. And leave us a comment to let us
know why you think Hollywood's given Fraser

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.439
the cold shoulder.

